> description: Extracts what the user actually wants through a one-question-at-a-time interview (~95% confidence) before any plan, spec, or code exists. Use ONLY when starting a NEW feature, new project, new report/presentation/paper/patent, or new screen, and who/why/success/constraint is missing so the direction would change; or when the user says "interview me" / "grill me". Do not use for bug fixes, small edits, legacy maintenance, pure questions, or non-interactive runs.
